# Environment: [Machine Name]

- machine: [friendly name, e.g., "laptop", "home-server"]
- hostname: [hostname]
- role: [interactive | background]
  - interactive: primary work machine, human present
  - background: always-on server, runs cron jobs, no human
- hardware: [model, RAM — helps Claude understand capabilities]
- services: [what runs here — e.g., "Obsidian GUI, iCloud Drive"]
- vaults: [which Obsidian vaults are on this machine]

## Role-specific behavior

### If interactive:
- Full UI access (Obsidian CLI, browser)
- MCP servers available for fallback
- Can prompt user for input

### If background:
- No UI, no browser, no user prompts
- Read from cached/synced data only
- Claude Code runs headless (`claude -p`)
- All output to log files
